  "cil_liability": false,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The application site is located within Flood Zone 2 and within an area identified as being at risk from surface water and fluvial flooding. The submitted Flood Risk Assessment fails to demonstrate that the proposed development, particularly the ground-floor bedrooms, would be safe from surface water and fluvial flooding over its lifetime, taking account of climate change. The proposal is therefore contrary to the relevant flood-risk provisions of the National Planning Policy Framework 2026, Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan 2021, Core Policy CP28 and Policies DMD 59, DMD 60 and DMD 61.",
    "The proposed development would fail to provide a satisfactory standard of accommodation for future occupiers. The communal kitchen/dining area due to its long and narrow layout would provide a poor, unsafe and impractical shared living space for six occupiers. Bedroom 2 would also be located directly adjacent to the communal ground floor kitchen/dining space and rear garden, resulting in undue noise and disturbance. The proposal would therefore fail to provide a high-quality form of shared accommodation, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework 2026, Policies D5 and D6 of the London Plan, Policy CP30 of the Core Strategy, and Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Development Management Document.",
    "The proposed development fails to provide adequate and policy-compliant cycle parking, by reason of the convoluted and impractical route through the dwelling and the absence of satisfactory external access. The proposal would therefore fail to provide a secure and convenient cycle parking facility and would not promote sustainable modes of transport, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework 2026, Policies T4 and T5 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy 25 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD45 and DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "In the absence of evidence to demonstrate that there is sufficient capacity to accommodate the parking demand, the proposed development would increase car parking pressure within the vicinity of the site, contrary to Policies DMD 5 and DMD 45 of the Development Management Document (2014) and Policies T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021)."
  ]
